From 2ac988f8835ebbc32ff438d8f8be435814cf2c7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 05:34:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test: optional-extra imports skip, not abort collection, in a
 minimal venv

`pytest tests/hermes_cli` stopped at collection in any venv without the `keychain` extra (the
hub's production venv): test_vault_key_cli.py imported `keyring` at module top, and one
collection error interrupts the whole session. Whole-tree collection had 149 such errors
(keyring, aiohttp, acp, plus one lark_oapi ordering bug).

- test_vault_key_cli.py and test_vault_key_storage.py: `keyring = pytest.importorskip("keyring")`.
- 87 aiohttp modules (gateway, e2e stand-ins, tui_gateway): module-level
  `pytest.importorskip("aiohttp.test_utils")` before the first aiohttp import. The probe is a
  submodule because other gateway tests stub sys.modules["aiohttp"] / ["aiohttp.web"] with a
  MagicMock when aiohttp is absent, and importorskip("aiohttp") would return that stub.
- 50 acp_adapter modules: `pytest.importorskip("acp")` before the first acp / acp_adapter import.
- test_feishu_{approval_buttons,card_action_gateway_authz}.py: check sys.modules before
  importlib.util.find_spec, which raises ValueError on a stub with no __spec__.

Test-only. CI installs these extras (tests.yml / tests-os.yml), so nothing skips there.
Hub production venv: `pytest --collect-only -q tests` 149 errors -> 0;
`pytest --collect-only -q tests/hermes_cli` rc 2 -> 0.
